            <ArticleTitle>[Right paraduodenal hernia: a case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>133-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Paraduodenal hernia is a rare etiology of intestinal obstruction. Its preoperative diagnosis can only be made by a well-performed upper gastrointestinal series. We report a case of a 19 years old man with abdominal pains and recurrent Koenig's syndromes. The upper gastrointestinal series and CT scan showed a right paraduodenal hernia. we reviewed the anatomy. physiopathology, symptoms and radiographic criteria for the diagnosis of the paraduodenal hernia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
